hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1120","Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “When one of you prays the two rak’ahs of dawn, let him lie on his right.” Then Marwan bin Al-Hakam said to him: Is not one of us sufficient? He walked to the mosque until he lay down. He said: This was reported to Ibn Umar, and he said: Abu Hurairah said more, so it was said to him: Do you disapprove of what he says? Something, he said: No, but he was bold, and we were cowardly, so this reached Abu Hurairah, and he said: What is my fault if I memorized it and they forgot?"
"1121","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ismail bin Aliya, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, who is Abu Maslamah, on the authority of Abu Nadra On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I visited my aunt, and it was the night before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned the hadith and said: “Then he prayed two rak’ahs, then He lay down until I heard his voice, then the prayer was performed and he went out and prayed.”"
